500:The channel-cost arbitrage (Section 8.7) arises because BASE_REWARDS are indexed by (action_type, situation), not channel: a context-blind EMAIL policy (EDUCATIONAL|EMAIL|bid 0.3) earns +$252.41, beating every deployable context-aware agent. We test a channel-dependent reward condition (`channel_mismatch_penalty = 0.5`): when the agent's channel differs from SITUATION_CHANNEL[situation], total reward is multiplied by 0.5. Results (50 seeds x 200 scenarios): cb_edu_email_030 drops from +$252.41 to +$132.72 (-47.5%), while cam_multisignal is nearly unchanged (+$206.13 -> +$205.77, -0.2%). The arbitrage disappears: cam_multisignal now beats cb_edu_email_030 by $73.05. situation_only (+$294.27) and oracle (+$210.00) are unaffected (they always use the correct channel). This confirms the arbitrage is a reward-design artifact, not a feature of context-aware decisioning.
504:To test whether the benchmark can falsify a wrong mapping (Section 9.2 #1), we construct an agent with perfect 3-signal classification (98.9% situational match) but a deranged action mapping (EXPLORATION->PROMOTIONAL, CONSIDERATION->CRISIS_RESPONSE, DECISION->EDUCATIONAL, CRISIS->LOYALTY, OPPORTUNITY->COMPARISON, RETENTION->URGENT). Results: 0.4% match against the true IDEAL_ACTION, profit -$268.88 (worse than the random baseline, -$170.03). The contrast vs cam_multisignal is +$475.01 (p = 5.23e-96, d = 29.28). Perfect classification with a wrong mapping is catastrophic, not merely suboptimal: the mapping itself carries the value, and the benchmark is falsifiable via profit.
524:The default crisis response is CRISIS_RESPONSE with a 2.0x bid multiplier (Section 6.5). We test three alternatives (Section 9.2 #23, Section 10.3 #17): pause (bid = 0.0), normal (bid = 1.0, no multiplier), and counter (2.0x, current default). Results (50 seeds x 200 scenarios): in the default environment, pause earns +$225.10, normal +$215.62, counter +$206.13. In the crisis_heavy environment (25% crisis situations), the gap widens: pause +$243.79, normal +$192.87, counter +$141.93. Pausing (bid = 0) is consistently better than counter-messaging (2.0x): the 2.0x crisis multiplier overbids in low-reward crisis situations. This finding does not invalidate the action mapping (CRISIS->CRISIS_RESPONSE is still correct) but suggests the bid multiplier should be calibrated, not hardcoded.
532:The §8.12 bandit baselines were **offline-trained** — the Agent ABC has no reward-feedback loop (§10.3 #12, §9.2 #13). Yet §8.11 showed the mapping itself carries the value. We therefore ask: **can an agent learn the situation→action mapping from observed profit alone, within a single 200-step episode?** Two online agents mirror `cam_multisignal` exactly — same 3-signal classifier, same channel rule (`SITUATION_CHANNEL[sit_est]`), same heuristic bid — and differ *only* in the action decision, which comes from a learned policy instead of the fixed `IDEAL_ACTION` table:
580:The pre-registered protocol of §10.3 #24, executed on 2026-11-02 (`paper/cam_sim_v15_llm.py`; results `results/cam_sim_v15.json`, response cache `results/llm_cache/`). Each context is textualized into a natural-language observation — intent strength, competitive density, channel quality, and the verbatim signals list *including the decoy `quality_score`* — and sent to an LLM at temperature 0 whose system prompt states the six situations as **qualitative marketing definitions only** (no numeric centroids, no examples; the full prompt is in the repo for audit). The returned label drives the same fixed pipeline as every CAM agent: `IDEAL_ACTION` action type, `SITUATION_CHANNEL` channel, oracle-style bid. The agent is therefore *identical to `cam_multisignal` except for the classifier* — any profit difference is attributable to classification quality alone. Evaluation runs on the identical per-seed context sequences (pairing-guard asserted against `run_online_env` byte-identically).
603:This v1.6 extension localizes the 8.21 blindness cause and tests remediation vs end-to-end agency. It is a strict pre-registration addition (item 24 follow-up), all numbers from `results/cam_sim_v16.md`, no fitted components, seed-level bootstrap CIs (10k reps, RNG 20261103). Eight arms: A order-permutation, B minimal-labels, C counterfactual-archetype probes, D decoy-removal, E qualitative-hints, F few-shot, G self-consistency, H end-to-end action selection. Arms A, B, C, D, G are descriptive diagnostics (no confirmatory claim); arms E, F, H carry inferential contrasts (profit means and model-vs-reference CIs).
605:**(A) Diagnostics — order, minimal-labels, decoy, self-consistency, counterfactual probes.** Arm A (Mistral, seed 1): six fixed permutations of the six class-definition blocks yield accuracy 86.5 / 86.5 / 86.5 / 86.5 / 84.0 / 86.5 — order-insensitive (max spread 2.5pp, same emission pattern). Arm B (minimal-labels, seed 1): Mistral 86.5% with definitions = 86.5% without — definitions contribute nothing to Mistral; glm-4.7 drops 83.0% (with definitions) → 74.0% (bare) — definitions matter for glm only. Arm D (decoy-removal, Mistral, seed 1): removing the decoy quality_score yields 86.5% with vs 86.5% without, delta exactly 0.0pp — decoy fully ignored. Arm G (self-consistency, seeds 1-5, crisis+retention contexts only, k=5 at temperature 0.7, majority vote): both families crisis recall 0/36 and retention recall 0/105, identical to zero-shot — sampling cannot rescue a prior collapse. Arm C (counterfactual archetypes, all five 8.21 models, 42 probes each = 210): synthetic observations at the six canonical centroids plus +/-0.15 scalar nudges. NO model EVER emits crisis or retention across all 210 probes, INCLUDING the exact crisis centroid (intent 0.8, competitive 0.85, quality 0.2 → all five say decision/consideration) and the exact retention centroid (0.3/0.15/0.8 → all say exploration). Blind spots are **prior-driven** emission collapse, not in-distribution discriminability failure: no scalar configuration induces the labels.
636:5. **`cam_inferred` is a structurally handicapped comparator:** its threshold rule can emit only 4 of 6 situation classes (never CRISIS or RETENTION), so its 75.7% match and distribution-shift collapse (F5) partly reflect a missing-class artifact. `cam_learned` (87.5%, emit-any-class) is the fairer intent-only comparator; the qualitative F5 story survives, but the magnitude is overstated by `cam_inferred`.

